  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADD Global - Policy advocacy on Alcohol, Drugs &amp; Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GAPA aims to reduce harm from alcohol use and improve achievement of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), including Goal 3 on health, and other goals related to gender and child rights. GAPA will engage in WHO processes related to alcohol policy; NCDs; and UHC and strengthen regional alcohol policy alliances. The programme relies heavily on research and evidence on public health oriented high-impact alcohol control policies and on collaboration between civil society actors and authorities. Across the world, alcohol systematically harms women to an extent that is disproportionate with their own use, due to men&#x2019;s drinking in a context of harmful masculinities and gender norms, as well as weakly regulated alcohol sales. Conversely, effective alcohol policies will disproportionately benefit women, and this is a core gender equality objective for GAPA&#x2019;s work. GAPA will commission scientific research and support the analysis and publication of findings comparing alcohol policy regulations and outcomes across different countries.</narrative>
  </description>
